                        <origDate when-custom="130X/131X" notBefore="1300" notAfter="1319"
                           calendar="#gregorian">s. xiv in.</origDate>
                     </origin>
                     <provenance type="#c"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_351">London.
                           Guildhall</orgName><p>BL, Cotton MS Claudius D. ii, fols 1–24, 30–40,
                           42–115, 124–135, 266–277, Guildhall, 'Liber Custumarum', fols. v,
                           1–84, 86–102, 173–186, and Oriel College, MS 46, fols 109–211, formed
                           one volume. Fols. 16–39 of the Corporation's 'Liber Albus' was
                           originally part of this MS, but was removed from it in the Middle
                           Ages.</p><p>Fols. 109–199 formerly foliated 215–304; fols 200–208
                           formerly foliated as 362–370. Fol. 209 is blank. Fol. 210r contains a
                           medieval table of contents with folio nos. Fol. 211 is an endleaf,
                           formerly foliated 37[.] (the last digit torn off). The table of contents
                           covers Guildhall, 'Liber Custumarum' fols. 1–102, 173–186, and Cotton
                           MS Claudius D. ii fols. 1–24, 31–115, 124–135, 266–277, of which this MS
                           was once part.</p><p>The medieval foliation has been obliterated. Traces
                           suggest that fols. 61–95 were formerly '45' to '79'.</p></provenance>
                     <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Cotton's arms on fol. [...].</provenance>
                  </history>
