                           calendar="#gregorian">s. xiv</origDate>
                     </origin>
                     <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="org_351">London.
                           Guildhall</orgName><p>Cotton Claudius D. ii, fols 116–123, Guildhall,
                           'Liber Custumarum', fols. 103–172, 187–286, and Oxford, Oriel College
                           46, fols. 1–108, formed one volume (i. e. quires ix--xvii of Oriel 46
                           now divided as Liber Custumarum fols. 103–172, 187–286 &amp; Claudius
                           D.ii fols. 116–123). This copy formerly part of the second part of the
                           Liber. Bequeathed to the Corporation by Andrew Horn 1328.</p><p>Medieval
                           foliation 'Lxx[ii]'--'Lxx[ix]'.</p></provenance>
                  </history>
